Stop this file instantiating what the bootloader already has: the slot
address tables, and the double-ECC fault handlers.

Both exist twice in ST's project because ST links TWO binaries, and ST's own
mechanism says so out loud -- sfu_fwimg_regions.h instantiates its const
tables only `#if defined(SFU_FWIMG_COMMON_C) || defined(SE_LOW_LEVEL_C) ||
defined(TEST_PROTECTIONS_C)`, which is how each image gets exactly one copy.
This rig links ONE ELF (B_L475E_IOT01A/2_Images_SECoreBin/Inc/se_low_level.h
has the reason), so both copies land in the same link and it fails with
`multiple definition of SlotStartAdd' and `multiple definition of
NMI_Handler'.

PORT_SINGLE_IMAGE is defined by the Makefile for every build this rig makes.

Hunk 1 -- the tables.  Dropping SE_LOW_LEVEL_C leaves the extern
declarations at the top of sfu_fwimg_regions.h in force and the definitions
to sfu_fwimg_common.c.  Both copies are `const` and both are built from the
same linker symbols, so there is no version of this where the two differ:
the SE core reads the same addresses either way.  -fcommon does not help
here and that is worth knowing -- these are INITIALISED definitions, and
-fcommon merges only tentative ones.

Hunk 2 -- the handlers.  KEEPING THE BOOTLOADER'S IS WHAT REPRODUCES ST'S
RUNTIME, not a coin toss.  The active vector table is the one at 0x08000000,
built from the SBSFU project's startup_stm32l475xx.s, and its NMI entry
resolves inside the SBSFU image -- so even in ST's two-binary build it is
sfu_low_level_flash_int.c's handler that runs, and the copy here sits in a
region VTOR never points at.

What does change: SE_DoubleECC_Error_Counter, which this file's handler
increments so SE code can discard a value read from a double-ECC-faulted
word, is never incremented.  That path needs an uncorrectable ECC error in
internal flash to be taken at all, and on a healthy part it is not -- and
with the handler gone such an event presents as the bootloader's own fault
path rather than as a silently wrong read.  It is recorded here rather than
left for someone to find in the symbol table.

HUNK 2'S GUARD OPENS ABOVE ST'S ATTRIBUTE BLOCK, not above the function.
The __attribute__((optimize("O1"))) four lines up applies to the next
declaration in the file, so a guard placed between it and NMI_Handler would
silently attach ST's optimisation override to whatever followed.  That is
the shape of the bug the L152 port's 0002 patch records, where an extern
dropped between a section attribute and its function moved the Secure
Engine's call gate out of its own region and the first SE call executed
linker padding.

Applied by the Makefile's STAGE_RULE -- this file is one of ST's project
sources rather than middleware -- with -F0, so if ST's lines ever move the
build stops rather than guarding the wrong region.
--- se_low_level.c
+++ se_low_level.c
@@ -18,7 +18,9 @@
   ******************************************************************************
   */
 
+#if !defined(PORT_SINGLE_IMAGE)
 #define SE_LOW_LEVEL_C
+#endif /* !PORT_SINGLE_IMAGE */
 
 /* Includes ------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 #include "se_low_level.h"
@@ -535,6 +537,7 @@
   return result;
 }
 
+#if !defined(PORT_SINGLE_IMAGE)
 /*
    As this handler code relies on stack pointer position to manipulate the PC return value, it is important
    not to use extra registers (on top of scratch registers), because it would change the stack pointer
@@ -625,6 +628,7 @@
 {
   SE_NMI_ExceptionHandler();
 }
+#endif /* !PORT_SINGLE_IMAGE */
 
